
================================================================================
                   THE ABANDONED LABORATORY
================================================================================

An abandoned laboratory of a wizard long dead.

A lone magickal torch ignites as you enter, shedding
light on the workshop, and casts haunting shadows
on every surface.

The flames lick the walls, burning off the moss that had
gathered there. The burning moss sizzles in the silence
of the catacombs, like angelic wailing or singing.

================================================================================
                    CHAINING SPELLS: Pipes
================================================================================

In the laboratory, the wizard's notes describe how to
CHAIN commands together, feeding the output of one spell
into another:

COMMAND                          PURPOSE
--------                         --------
cmd1 | cmd2                      Pipe: output of cmd1 feeds into cmd2
cat scroll | grep "wizard"       Find lines containing "wizard"
ls | wc -l                       Count how many items are in a room

These "pipes" are one of the most powerful tools in the
terminal. They let you combine simple commands into
complex operations.

Try examining the ghost before you face it:

    $ file ghost
    $ cat ghost | head -20

================================================================================
                       NAVIGATION
================================================================================

    ./ghost          Face the ghost (if you dare!)
